\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Hear us, O Lord, from heaven, Thy dwelling- place:
\par Like them of old, in vain we toil all night,
\par Unless with us Thou go, who art the Light;
\par Come then, O Lord, that we may see Thy face.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou, Lord, dost rule the raging of the sea,
\par When loud the storm and furious is the gale:
\par Strong is Thine arm; our little barques are frail:
\par Send us Thy help; remember Galilee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Our wives and children we commend to Thee:
\par For them we plough the land and plough the deep;
\par For them by day the golden corn we reap,
\par By night the silver harvest of the sea.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. We thank Thee, Lord, for sunshine, dew, and rain,
\par Broadcast from heaven by Thine  almighty hand-
\par Source of all life, unnumbered as the sand-
\par Bird, beast, and fish, herb, fruit, and golden grain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O Bread of Life, Thou in Thy word hast said:
\par Who feeds in faith on Me shall never die!
\par In mercy hear Thy hungry children's cry:
\par Father, give us this day our daily bread!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Sow in our hearts the seeds of Thy dear love,
\par That we may reap contentment, joy, and peace;
\par And when at last our earthly labours cease;
\par Grant us to join Thy harvest home above.
\par              Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

